# argus's secrets. Copy this to .env and fill it in — `./scripts/bootstrap.sh env` does
# both, prompting without echo and leaving the file mode 600. .env is gitignored and Bun
# loads it for every `bun …` script, so nothing is exported into the shell and no other
# process — every Claude session on the machine included — inherits a token by accident.
#
# The upstream keys live here once. slack-pull reads SLACK_TOKEN; the MCP gateway
# (infra/compose.yaml, `./scripts/bootstrap.sh mcp`) gets SLACK_TOKEN and LINEAR_API_KEY
# through compose's --env-file and serves Slack's and Linear's MCP servers to every Claude
# session, which presents MCP_GATEWAY_TOKEN instead of a key.
#
# SLACK_TOKEN  slack-digest's slack-pull.ts, and so the sweep's digest tick.
#              Scopes: channels:history + users:read (a user token also needs
#              channels:read).

SLACK_TOKEN=

# LINEAR_API_KEY  the gateway's Linear server. A personal API key: linear.app → Settings →
#              Security & access → Personal API keys.

LINEAR_API_KEY=

# MCP_GATEWAY_TOKEN  what a Claude session in this checkout presents to the MCP gateway
#              (mcp-proxy on :9090), which serves Linear's and Slack's hosted MCP servers
#              as .mcp.json's `linear` and `slack`. scripts/mcp-headers.ts reads it from
#              here for the headersHelper; the gateway holds the upstream keys and a
#              session never sees them. `bootstrap.sh mcp` mints it when absent;
#              Foundry's FOUNDRY_MCP_TOKEN holds the same value for its forges.

MCP_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# argus reads Bitbucket pipelines to know whether a backend landing deployed. It uses the
# credentials bb keeps in ~/.bitbucket-rest-cli-config.json; set this to point elsewhere.
BITBUCKET_CONFIG=
